Review_comment:
The aim of the paper is to increase the efficiency of the control quality of management systems. 
It is an interesting project, and relatively new, the use of AI is not a novelty in optimization processes, but good implemented. In this case, the authors proposal the development of a Implementing Models and Algorithms for Digital Transformation of Documentation Support for Quality Management System to detect Contradictions and Inconsistencies in Documentation Support of Quality Management System (QMS) of Kazakhstan Economy.  The results presented in the article describe this as a novelty and are valid in the context of the presented project.
As a result of reviewing the article I recommend the article for publication with minor (technical) corrections «Accepted with minor revision».

- it is necessary to issue an article according to a template:
•	paper title(In the paper title, capitalize the first letter of the first and last word and all the nouns, pronouns, adjectives, verbs, adverbs, and subordinating conjunctions);
•	abstract should start from the word “Abstract-“	;
•	keywords (list keywords separated by semicolons);
•	figures (Place figures and tables after they are first cited in the text. Use the abbreviation “Fig. 1”, even at the beginning of a sentence, correct the description of the drawings according to the format: Figure 1. Figure caption);
•	references (Capitalize only the first word in a paper title, except for proper nouns and element symbols).
- the article must be written from the third person. It is not allowed to use the pronoun "we", etc.
- references should be no later than 5-7 years from the current year.

I recommend accepting this work with minor modifications:
1) Formulas need to be written in Equation, not as figures;
2) Give a title to each figure and Sections of the y-axis are not visible in some figures

The authors introduce the advanced modeling approaches and demonstrate their usability for practical problem of managing heat supply. The developed models were applied to represent operation of boiler plants and predict heating demand and have been validated agains the measurements data. An inter-model comparison has been done both in terms of accuracy and considering insights which can be obtained using each of the approaches. The results of the work are novel, practically relevant and fit well into the conference agenda. The work is presented in a clear and consistent way, although the text could additionally benefit from being a bit more structured to facilitate reading.

The paper may be definitely recommended for publication after some minor adjustments:
1) double-check typos in the text and explanations for all the abbreviations;
2)  fix formatting of the title and equations when needed;
3) checking that all the digits in the numeric results are meaningful.

The work is aimed to analyze from the first principles a flow in a system of a certain geometry. That is a potentially very fruitful approach especially when combining the theoretical analysis with validation against experimental data and computational modeling, as the Author suggests. However, the Author does not explain which exactly application is considered and what is a contribution of the presented work. That makes judgment on work novelty and relevance quite difficult as there are a lot of well-studied hydrodynamic applications for incompressible single phase flows in pipelines of various geometry. It seems from the paper conclusion that the work is aimed to model blood movement in arteries and veins. This application could be novel and of high practical importance. Whether that is the case in fact, is unfortunately not clear from the paper. 

It may be recommended to revise presentation of the work to clearly explain:
1) which practical problem should be solved by this work;
2) what is state-of-the-art of research on the considered problem (even a brief literature review on the problem in question would be very helpful for a reader to understand the context and novelty of the work);
3) what is an intended contribution of the work.

- Abstract and other part: need to moderate;
- Introduction: The introduction does not contain a clear statement of the research aim. There is a lack of literature review on the research topic;
- It is recommended to disclose the research methodology.
Number equations consecutively with equation numbers in parentheses flush with the right margin, as in (1);
- some equations are not displayed correctly;
- Requirements for the submitted work in relation to citation are not met.

Do Not Use Symbols, Special Characters, or Math in  Abstract.
The paper needs reworking the abstract;
Some equations are displayed incorrectly;
Add a literature review on the research topic.

The article "Development of a Digital Stethoscopy System for Detection of Heart Diseases" is relevant and has valuable practical significance.
Disadvantages of work:
- it is necessary to mathematically describe the operation of the stethoscope presented in the article;
- add information about the machine learning model that will be used in "Digital Stethoscopy System", a software environment for machine learning;
- describe the software offered in "Digital Stethoscopy System";
- describe the scientific novelty of the article;
- add quantitative data, for example, model accuracy.
The work can be accepted after revision.
